{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/authoramish/videos/in-the-1890s-two-indian-police-officers-made-a-remarkable-contribution-to-the-hi/1841919220168664/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/authoramish/videos/in-the-1890s-two-indian-police-officers-made-a-remarkable-contribution-to-the-hi/1841919220168664/","title":"33K views · 929 reactions | In the 1890s, two Indian police officers made a remarkable contribution to the history of fingerprint identification.\n\nQazi Azizul Haque and Hem Chandra Bose developed classification methods that helped police organise and identify fingerprints more efficiently.\n\nTheir work revolutionised criminal identification, with police forces around the world adopting the system.\n\nWhat makes their contribution even more remarkable is that their work helped lay the foundation for modern forensic fingerprint identification systems.\n\n.\n.\n.\n\n#FingerprintHistory #IndianScience #ForensicScience #IndianHistory #AmishTripathi | Amish Tripathi","description":"In the 1890s, two Indian police officers made a remarkable contribution to the history of fingerprint identification.\n\nQazi Azizul Haque and Hem Chandra Bose developed classification methods that...","language":"en","text":"And so, the Ramayan travelled across the Indian Ocean, reaching cultures far beyond India.\nCarried by Indian traders and travellers, its stories and traditions found a home in distant lands, connecting civilisations across oceans.\nDiscover more in the full episode of Ramayan Beyond Borders, now on YouTube.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2456.013985996833,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}